-mechanical scan and recognizing the deliberately nested clique blocks.
 
-Generation.  A clique K is sampled first.  The remaining vertices are split
-into two cliques C0,C1 with no edges between them.  Each outside vertex receives
-a threshold t in {1,...,|K|}; after ordering K as k1,...,kk, it is adjacent to
-ki exactly when i>t.  Thus every K-to-Cj neighborhood is nested.  K is a known
-hitting clique because deleting it leaves C0 disjoint from C1.  The graph is
-chordal: an induced cycle cannot use both outside cliques (two K vertices would
-give a chord), and within K union Cj nested cross-neighborhoods forbid an
-induced C4.  Every induced P3 meets K, so two disjoint induced P3s have an edge
-between their K vertices; hence the graph is induced-2P3-free.  A final uniform
-vertex relabelling removes positional information.  Seed-dependent block sizes
-and threshold multiplicities give genuinely non-isomorphic instances.
