The existing construction is mathematically promising and uses the paper’s own Proposition 18 reduction rather than the prior triage’s unsupported “plant arbitrary clusters” idea. Its certificate is inverse-generated and exact: a parity hyperplane is a vertex cover of a succinct Cayley graph, a generator matching proves optimality, and Proposition 18 carries that optimum to Cluster Vertex Deletion. I’m auditing two remaining risk points before editing: the paper’s exact complexity/easy-regime statements, and whether the claimed 215-operation compact route honestly satisfies the no-tool cap.
