 ## Caveats
 
-The construction becomes easy as soon as the solver notices and accurately
-executes the all-generator XOR; that is intentional Track B behavior. The G4
-density is under a uniform prior over nonzero parity functionals and a side bit;
-it says nothing about a solver prior biased toward XOR combinations. Gaussian
-elimination was run and succeeds, as expected. No SAT/SMT or generic explicit-
-graph Cluster-VD implementation was run—the graph has `2^73` vertices at the
-shipping preset and is intentionally succinct. The checker validates the finite
-symbolic certificate rather than expanding that graph. `canonical_key` uses a
-four-circuit incidence invariant, not a complete matroid-isomorphism canonizer,
-so rare non-isomorphic collisions remain possible despite the 20/20 test. The
-largest caveat is decisive: the four-vendor hardening and all G9 diagnostics are
-still unmeasured because the configured OpenRouter key has exhausted its total
-limit.
+- This is a succinct graph, not the paper’s usual explicit adjacency input. The
+  pendant reduction is central to Proposition 18, but the finite-field Cayley
+  source graph is generator-specific.
+- A tool makes the family easy: Gaussian elimination took milliseconds. This is
+  exactly why the declaration is Track B, never Track A.
+- The compact route still requires 215 exact 72-bit XORs at `easy`, close to the
+  300-operation cap. Failures may partly measure exact arithmetic stamina even
+  after the invariant is found.
+- The G4 prior is uniform over every stated nonzero functional and side. Its tiny
+  density does not model a solver biased toward XORs of visible masks.
+- SAT/ILP, Sherali-Adams, and the paper’s explicit-graph approximation were not
+  materialised on a `2^73`-vertex graph. The specialized exact linear solver is
+  the strongest applicable reference attack actually run.
+- `canonical_key` uses short GF(2)-dependence invariants. It is invariant under
+  tested affine relabellings but is not a complete Cayley-graph isomorphism test,
+  so unobserved collisions remain possible.
+- Most importantly, the oracle pool and all G9 arms are unscored because the
+  supplied OpenRouter key hit its total limit. Re-run all three arms before
+  trusting or submitting the hardness claim.
