codex
Implemented a Track B generator based on the paper’s Proposition 18 pendant-edge reduction. The certificate is a compact parity-hyperplane description; exact Gaussian elimination costs 474,459 scalar-bit operations, while the intended XOR invariant uses 215 operations. The paper and reduction were verified against the [full arXiv paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2007.08057).

Deliverables:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2007.08057/gen_2007_08057.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2007.08057/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2007.08057/README.md)
- [Bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2007.08057/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2007.08057/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2007.08057/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

All local gates pass, including 0/200,000 random hits, four attacks at 0/8, reference elimination at 8/8, and 20/20 distinct canonical keys.

The result is not submission-ready: OpenRouter rejected every oracle request with HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded,” so no hardness verdict or G9 comparison could be measured. The authentic error transcripts are preserved. Replenishing the configured OpenRouter key and rerunning `harden.py` is the only remaining blocker.
