All local gates pass: 16/16 planted checks, 0/200,000 random-guess hits, four attacks at 0/8, exact reference algorithm at 8/8, and 140/140 canonical relabelling checks. The construction and cited regimes were verified against the [full arXiv paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2007.08057).

One requirement remains externally blocked: all official oracle calls returned OpenRouter HTTP 403 “key limit exceeded,” yielding zero valid attempts. Consequently, there is no `hardened` verdict and the result is not ready for submission until STEP 4 is rerun with a replenished key. The error transcripts and this limitation are documented honestly in the README.
